- New method `async gerarLinkRedefinicaoSenha(motoboyId, restaurantId)`: verify ownership via `exigirMotoboyGerenciadoPeloRestaurante`, fetch the motoboy's `email`/`user_id` (404 if no `user_id` — can't generate a link for a motoboy who was never migrated), call `this.supabase.client.auth.admin.generateLink({ type: 'recovery', email })`, return `{ link: data.properties.action_link }` for the frontend to build the WhatsApp deep link / copy button.
- New method `async enviarLinkRedefinicaoSenhaPorEmail(motoboyId, restaurantId)`: verify ownership, fetch `email`, call `this.supabase.client.auth.resetPasswordForEmail(email, { redirectTo: ... })` — **note**: `resetPasswordForEmail` is a client-side-shaped call (uses the public/anon-style auth API, not `admin.*`); check whether `SupabaseService`'s client (service-role key) can call `.auth.resetPasswordForEmail` server-side. It can — `supabase-js`'s `.auth.resetPasswordForEmail` works with any client regardless of which key it was constructed with, since it hits the public `/auth/v1/recover` endpoint, not an admin-only one. This reuses the exact mechanism `authService.resetPassword` already uses client-side for customers, satisfying "no custom mailer" constraint.

